<DocsLayout title="Memory & Sessions" description="How lean-ctx persists context across sessions: CCP, knowledge, episodic memory, and session survival.">
  <h1>Memory & Sessions</h1>
  <p>lean-ctx remembers context across sessions. When your AI starts a new conversation, it can recover previous state, knowledge, and decisions automatically.</p>

  <h2>Session State</h2>
  <p>Every lean-ctx session tracks:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Files accessed</strong> — what was read, which mode, when</li>
    <li><strong>Task context</strong> — current objectives, findings, blockers</li>
    <li><strong>Decisions</strong> — architectural choices made during the session</li>
    <li><strong>Compression checkpoints</strong> — context snapshots for recovery</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Session Commands</h3>
  <pre><code>ctx_session(action="status")     # Current session state
ctx_session(action="save")       # Persist session
ctx_session(action="load")       # Restore previous session
ctx_session(action="compress")   # Create checkpoint</code></pre>

  <h2>Context Continuity Protocol (CCP)</h2>
  <p>CCP ensures that when context is compacted (by the AI tool or by reaching limits), lean-ctx can reconstruct the essential state from structured recovery queries.</p>
  <p>The session survival engine stores:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Active file refs (F1, F2, F3...)</li>
    <li>Recent tool calls and results</li>
    <li>Pending tasks and decisions</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Project Knowledge (AAAK)</h2>
  <p>Persistent facts about the project that survive across all sessions:</p>
  <pre><code>ctx_knowledge(action="remember", key="db_schema", value="PostgreSQL, schema in migrations/")
ctx_knowledge(action="recall", key="db_schema")
ctx_knowledge(action="search", value="database")</code></pre>

  <p>Knowledge facts are temporal — they track when they were learned and can be superseded by newer information.</p>

  <h2>Episodic Memory</h2>
  <p>Records significant events during coding sessions (errors, breakthroughs, decisions) for later retrieval:</p>
  <pre><code>ctx_session(action="episodes", value="record")
ctx_session(action="episodes", value="search auth bug")</code></pre>

  <h2>Procedural Memory</h2>
  <p>Detects repeated patterns in your workflow and suggests optimized procedures:</p>
  <pre><code>ctx_session(action="procedures", value="detect")
ctx_session(action="procedures", value="suggest refactor")</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
